cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below. You are never required to cite it to use or teach from it."
title: "Python Foundations for the Life Sciences"
abstract: >-
  A beginner-level open course teaching Python through real biological data: FASTA
  parsing, composition statistics, quality control and reproducible reporting, with a
  tested teaching package (seqreport), three 13-part lessons, five guided practicals,
  three assignments, two challenges and an instructor pack. Part of the CLS-Open
  initiative of fifteen interlinked computational life-sciences courses.
